> write a cover letter for this job: bStart
> LabStart is a nonprofit deep climate technology venture studio backing climate solutions that are too early, too hard, or too important to ignore.
> We work hands-on with seasoned entrepreneurs, first-time founders, and industry experts to launch fundable, high-impact ventures. From lab to launch, we provide the earliest support—bridging the gap between breakthrough innovation and investable startup.
> Our lean, mission-driven team is backed by catalytic funders who believe in moving faster, funding smarter, and building a more inclusive climate future.
> The Role
> LabStart is seeking a Fundraising Development Lead to serve as the engine of our growth. This role is a hybrid of strategic relationship management and proactive business development.
> We aren't starting from scratch - you will inherit a qualified, researched pipeline of funders, and we need a strategic connector to activate and refine those leads while simultaneously scouting for the next wave of partners. You will be responsible for the full lifecycle of a donor: from initial research and "cold" outreach to long-term stewardship.
> Key Responsibilities
> Full-Cycle Relationship Management: Transition warm, researched prospects through the cultivation cycle, from first contact to closing and long-term stewardship.
> New Lead Generation: Use your "hunter" instincts to identify, qualify, and reach out to new philanthropic prospects that align with LabStart’s mission.
> Proactive Growth: Identify and bridge gaps in our current network, utilizing research tools and industry networking to keep the pipeline consistently full.
> Presence & Advocacy: Act as a primary ambassador for LabStart at key industry events (e.g., Climate Week, investor summits). You are comfortable navigating diverse environments, from family office boardrooms to tech-forward mixers.
> Data-Driven Development: Own the fundraising "engine." Use our CRM (Monday.com) to track engagement metrics, ensuring timely follow-ups and transparent reporting for the leadership team.
> Strategic Storytelling: Collaborate with the team to translate climate-tech initiatives into compelling opportunities for philanthropic and catalytic capital.
> Commitment to Relationship Longevity: You understand that the best partnerships aren't built in a quarter. You are looking for a 3+ year horizon where you can steward relationships from the initial introduction to long-term, multi-cycle support.
> Qualifications
> 5–7 years of experience in nonprofit development, venture capital relations, or high-end sales.
> You possess the emotional intelligence (EQ) to build immediate rapport and the organizational discipline to manage a complex, multi-stage pipeline.
> Authenticity and integrity – with both the donor world and the internal team
> You have a high "rejection-to-success" tolerance and the relentless tenacity skills required to get onto a busy donor's calendar.
> You are autonomous, extremely organized, and genuinely excited about the intersection of climate tech and philanthropic capital.  Small teams excite you.
> Location: NY or SF preferred, others considered on a case-by-case basis
> Preferred Qualifications
